   "id": "culture-etiquette-and-holidays",
   "title": "Culture, etiquette and holidays",
   "body": "A few habits make daily life smoother, and the holiday calendar matters because offices and banks close and trains sell out during the long breaks ([CLI, updated October 2026](https://studycli.org/chinese-holidays/2027/)).\n**Etiquette basics**\n- Greetings: a nod or handshake; say 你好 (nǐ hǎo). Use titles with surnames for teachers, e.g. 王老师 (Teacher Wang).\n- Meals: dishes are shared; don't stick chopsticks upright in rice; the host often pays, and offering to pay is polite.\n- Gifts: give and receive with both hands; avoid clocks and sets of four. Fruit or snacks from home are good gifts for teachers and hosts.\n- Tipping: not expected.\n- Bargaining: normal in markets, not in malls, supermarkets or apps.\n- Queues and crowds: expect pushing at busy stations; stay patient.\n- Face (面子): avoid criticising someone in public; raise problems privately and politely.\n- WeChat is used for everything, including teachers and landlords; reply politely and avoid voice messages to people you don't know well.\n**Public holidays 2027 (expected; official schedule due around November 2026)**\n\n| Holiday | Expected days off | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| New Year's Day | Jan 1–3 |  |\n| Spring Festival (春节) | Feb 5–12 (New Year Feb 6) | Biggest travel rush (春运) about Jan 22–Mar 2; many small shops close; book trains early |\n| Qingming (清明节) | Apr 3–5 | Tomb-sweeping |\n| Labor Day (劳动节) | May 1–5 | Very busy travel week |\n| Dragon Boat (端午节) | Jun 9 | Zongzi and boat races |\n| Mid-Autumn (中秋节) | Sep 15 | Mooncakes, family dinners |\n| National Day (国庆节) | Oct 1–7 | Golden Week; tourist sites very crowded |\n\nThe State Council also swaps some weekends into workdays (调休) around long holidays, so the agent should check the official notice before telling users which days are free. Government offices and banks close for the whole break.\n**Agent tips:** remind students about Spring Festival tickets about two weeks before travel, and warn that Exit-Entry and bank tasks cannot be done during Golden Weeks."
