   "id": "weather-and-climate-by-region",
   "title": "Weather and climate by region",
   "body": "China's climate ranges from cold, dry winters in the north to warm weather all year in the far south; the agent uses this to match places to a user's home climate and to warn about seasons. For exact temperatures, it should call a live weather API (such as QWeather, 和风天气) rather than rely on this summary, which is general knowledge, not measured data.\n\n| Region | Example cities | Winter | Summer | Notes for newcomers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| North | Beijing, Tianjin, Xi'an | Cold, dry, below freezing | Hot | Indoor central heating in winter; dry air and dust in spring |\n| Northeast | Harbin, Shenyang, Changchun | Very cold, snow | Warm, short | Ice festivals; needs heavy winter clothing |\n| East and Central | Shanghai, Nanjing, Hangzhou, Wuhan | Cold and damp | Hot and humid; rainy season around June | Many homes south of the Huai River have no central heating; use air-conditioners or heaters |\n| South | Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Xiamen | Mild | Hot, humid, typhoons in late summer | Closest to East African coastal weather |\n| Tropical south | Sanya (Hainan) | Warm | Hot | Beaches; good escape in winter |\n| Southwest | Kunming, Dali | Mild all year | Mild | Kunming is called the \"Spring City\" |\n| Sichuan Basin | Chengdu, Chongqing | Cool, cloudy | Hot, humid | Famous spicy food |\n| Northwest | Urumqi, Lanzhou | Cold, dry | Hot, dry | Large day–night swings |\n\n**Climate matching examples**\n- From warm, humid coasts (e.g. Dar es Salaam, Mombasa, Lagos): Guangzhou, Shenzhen, Xiamen and Sanya feel most familiar; Kunming suits people who like mild highland weather (e.g. Arusha, Nairobi).\n- From cold countries: Beijing, Harbin or Shenyang winters will feel normal.\n**Agent tips:** warn students from warm countries before their first winter in central or northern China, suggest buying winter clothes on Taobao or Pinduoduo in October, and mention heaters for dorms without central heating."
